  "result": "The U-turn concept is written and the gate passed it with **`OK`** on the first run (1 of 6 used). It reported \"3 witnesses, 1 names, reads 1 atom(s)\".\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/u_turn.lean`): at each moment, the size of the heading change over the window behind it must be at least `min_angle` and at most `max_angle`, both ends included.\n- I measure the turn with the record's one claimed measurement, `prim_heading_change`, and take its absolute value so a turn to either hand counts.\n- A vehicle that only backs up has no heading change, so the result is false.\n- When the window reaches back before the start of the recording, or a yaw rate is missing, the measurement itself returns unknown, which is what the contract asks for.\n- The contract left nothing open to interpretation, so I recorded no narrowings.\n\n**The test cases** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/u_turn.lean`), using a 10 s window and a 160°–200° band:\n- **holds:** a car makes a three-point turn (forward, reverse, forward) at 30°/s, for 180° in total. It is judged at t = 15–19 s, when the whole turn is inside the window.\n- **fails:** a car backs west for 12 s without turning. It is judged at t = 10–12 s, the first moments with a full 10 s of history.\n- **blind:** the same trace as `holds`, with the yaw-rate measurement marked absent.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
